WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.908 --> 00:00:03.746
- [Host] Pop quiz
hotshot, you're in Harlem

00:00:03.746 --> 00:00:05.030
and you're at this building.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.086
You go through the door,
enter the security code,

00:00:07.086 --> 00:00:08.995
take the elevator to the third floor,

00:00:08.995 --> 00:00:11.501
knock on this door where Rudy greets you.

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:13.459
- Hi and welcome.
- You make your way

00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:16.570
into a packed apartment
and try to find a seat.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.164
What do you get?

00:00:18.164 --> 00:00:19.681
(jazz music)

00:00:19.681 --> 00:00:23.514
You get a live jazz
performance like no other.

00:00:27.249 --> 00:00:30.448
(applauding)

00:00:30.448 --> 00:00:32.878
Every Sunday, Marjorie Eliot
and her son Rudel Drears

00:00:32.878 --> 00:00:34.718
open the doors to their
apartment for people

00:00:34.718 --> 00:00:36.635
to come and listen to jazz music.

00:00:36.635 --> 00:00:38.657
- We decided to use our apartment because

00:00:38.657 --> 00:00:41.918
we can do what we want here. (laughing)

00:00:41.918 --> 00:00:43.802
It's just a matter of this is home.

00:00:43.802 --> 00:00:45.612
So everybody who walks through that door,

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.020
we treat as family.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.440
- [Host] And it's a pretty big family.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.912
The concerts are so popular
that if you're not on time,

00:00:50.912 --> 00:00:53.104
finding a seat can be a little tricky.

00:00:53.104 --> 00:00:56.334
- We fill up the living room,
the kitchen, the hallway,

00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:58.480
and people just stand out taking videos.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.793
It's pretty much like
that every Sunday now.

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:02.126
It's jam packed.

00:01:03.119 --> 00:01:06.540
(mournful jazz music)

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.413
- [Host] The jazz concerts began in 1993

00:01:08.413 --> 00:01:11.109
after Rudel's brother Phil passed away.

00:01:11.109 --> 00:01:13.651
- Well, my brother passed away on a Sunday

00:01:13.651 --> 00:01:16.540
and mama had the great idea to honor him

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:18.186
with concerts on Sundays.

00:01:18.186 --> 00:01:22.643
You know, when you play music, you
just get all your angst out

00:01:22.643 --> 00:01:25.028
and it's just a healing feeling.

00:01:25.028 --> 00:01:28.496
So, I think her thing was, you know,
what better way to honor him

00:01:28.496 --> 00:01:29.838
than with a concert?

00:01:29.838 --> 00:01:32.384
And we've been blessed to
never have missed a Sunday.

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:34.771
(applauding)

00:01:34.771 --> 00:01:37.398
(upbeat jazz music)

00:01:37.398 --> 00:01:38.964
- [Host] With their
commitment and consistency

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:41.043
to play every Sunday, the concerts are now

00:01:41.043 --> 00:01:43.580
considered legendary in
Harlem, attracting audiences

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.241
from all over the world.

00:01:45.241 --> 00:01:46.903
Hey Rudel, do you mind if we ask some of

00:01:46.903 --> 00:01:48.565
the audience members where they came from?

00:01:48.565 --> 00:01:49.901
- Of course.
- I'm from Germany.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.219
- France.
- Australia.

00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:53.158
- Colombia.
- That's pretty cool.

00:01:53.158 --> 00:01:57.168
♪ Oh when the saints, oh when the saints ♪

00:01:57.168 --> 00:02:00.870
♪ Go marching in, go marching in ♪

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.740
- [Rudel] I think once we
started it just took on

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.196
a life force of its own.

00:02:04.196 --> 00:02:05.737
Sometimes people come and they just,

00:02:05.737 --> 00:02:07.426
they don't know what they're gonna expect.

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:10.409
You know, it's like, ring
a bell and get free jazz?

00:02:10.409 --> 00:02:13.159
And then once they get here,
they have that experience,

00:02:13.159 --> 00:02:16.576
it's kind of something they won't forget.

00:02:20.962 --> 00:02:22.491
For some people this is their church.

00:02:22.491 --> 00:02:24.530
People come here and they feel renewed.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:26.716
And we feel renewed.

00:02:26.716 --> 00:02:29.496
And you never know who
you're gonna touch out there.

00:02:29.496 --> 00:02:33.135
So, if you're putting out
good energy, it's gonna work.

00:02:33.135 --> 00:02:37.302
(audience exclaiming and applauding)

